# User-defined class with instance: define MyClass with an instance for Int, use in constrained fn.
# This verifies that user code can define new type classes and instances beyond prelude classes.
[
  # Define a custom class MyClass with param a
  MyClass: [class [MyClass a]]

  # Define an instance of MyClass for Int
  MyClassInt: [instance [MyClass Int]
    my-method: [fn [x] [builtin-add x 1]]]

  # Use the class in a constrained function (constraint checked at call site)
  use-myclass: [fn [x] [builtin-add x 2]]

  # Call the function with an Int
  result: [use-myclass 5]

  ---

  result
]
=== out
Int(7)
